    "case_id": "amb1-case02-nonprofit-scale",
    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne049\tWillow Hub says we could start with one evening every other week rather than weekly.\ne050\tThat sounds like a pilot, but our current volunteers say irregular scheduling is harder, not easier.\ne051\tParticipants may also assume it is permanent once we advertise it.\ne052\tThe community center wants an answer within three weeks because they are planning their calendar.\ne053\tI feel pressure to call a smaller launch reversible when socially it may not be.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne054\tYou are right that operational smallness does not guarantee social reversibility.\ne055\tA limited schedule can still create expectations and consume trust if it disappears.\ne056\tThe pilot would need an honest duration, a clear decision date, and a credible promise about what happens to participants if it ends.\ne057\tEven then, ending could disappoint people.\ne058\tThe point is not to make withdrawal painless; it is to avoid describing a permanent service before you know you can sustain one.",
      "citation_allowed": true,
